### 1.  Moles of CO that pass through the reactor in 1 h  

The flow rate of CO is  

\[
v_{\mathrm{CO}} = 0.01\ \mathrm{dm^{3}\,min^{-1}} = 0.01\ \mathrm{L\,min^{-1}}
\]

At the given temperature and pressure the molar volume of an ideal gas is  

\[
V_{\mathrm{m}}=\frac{RT}{P}= \frac{8.314\ \mathrm{J\,K^{-1}\,mol^{-1}}\times273.15\ \mathrm{K}}
{101325\ \mathrm{Pa}}=22.414\ \mathrm{L\,mol^{-1}}
\]

Hence the moles of CO introduced per minute are  

\[
n_{\mathrm{CO,min}}=\frac{v_{\mathrm{CO}}}{V_{\mathrm{m}}}
= \frac{0.01\ \mathrm{L\,min^{-1}}}{22.414\ \mathrm{L\,mol^{-1}}}
=4.46\times10^{-4}\ \mathrm{mol\,min^{-1}}
\]

In one hour (60 min):

\[
n_{\mathrm{CO,total}} = 4.46\times10^{-4}\ \mathrm{mol\,min^{-1}}\times60
=2.68\times10^{-2}\ \mathrm{mol}
\]

---

### 2.  Moles of CO actually converted to CO₂  

The conversion efficiency is \(\eta = 70\% = 0.70\).

\[
n_{\mathrm{CO_2}} = \eta\, n_{\mathrm{CO,total}}
=0.70 \times 2.68\times10^{-2}
=1.87\times10^{-2}\ \mathrm{mol}
\]

Each converted CO molecule yields one CO₂ molecule, so this is also the amount of CO₂ formed.

---

### 3.  Number of CO₂ molecules produced  

\[
N_{\mathrm{CO_2}} = n_{\mathrm{CO_2}}\,N_{\!A}
=1.87\times10^{-2}\ \mathrm{mol}\times6.022\times10^{23}\ \mathrm{mol^{-1}}
\approx 1.13\times10^{22}\ \text{molecules}
\]

---

### 4.  Number of Pd atoms that are on the surface  

Mass of Pd in the catalyst:

\[
m_{\mathrm{Pd}} = w_{\mathrm{Pd}}\;m_{\mathrm{cat}} =0.10\times0.10\ \mathrm{g}=0.010\ \mathrm{g}
\]

Moles of Pd:

\[
n_{\mathrm{Pd}} = \frac{m_{\mathrm{Pd}}}{M_{\mathrm{Pd}}}
= \frac{0.010\ \mathrm{g}}{106.42\ \mathrm{g\,mol^{-1}}}
=9.40\times10^{-5}\ \mathrm{mol}
\]

Total Pd atoms:

\[
N_{\mathrm{Pd,total}} = n_{\mathrm{Pd}}\,N_{\!A}
=9.40\times10^{-5}\ \mathrm{mol}\times6.022\times10^{23}\ \mathrm{mol^{-1}}
\approx 5.66\times10^{19}\ \text{atoms}
\]

Only 10 % of these atoms are exposed on the surface:

\[
N_{\mathrm{Pd,surf}} = 0.10 \times N_{\mathrm{Pd,total}}
\approx 5.66\times10^{18}\ \text{surface Pd atoms}
\]

---

### 5.  CO₂ molecules formed per surface Pd atom  

\[
N = \frac{N_{\mathrm{CO_2}}}{N_{\mathrm{Pd,surf}}}
= \frac{1.13\times10^{22}}{5.66\times10^{18}}
\approx 2.0\times10^{3}
\]

---

\[
\boxed{N \approx 2.0\times10^{3}\ \text{CO}_2\ \text{molecules per surface Pd atom after 1 h}}
\]
